Class AACommRemoteFpgaInfo (AAComm.Extensions; AAComm C#): Helper class used to read and validate Master Remote Unit FPGA RPD (data) and VER (version) files. Class instance is passed as an argument toStartDownloading Make sure to set the correct Port
Signature: class AAComm.Extensions.AACommRemoteFpgaInfo

Members:
- ctor .ctor(System.String)
  Reads the RPD (MAX10) or BIN (PH1P) data file and its VER version file, and initializes the properties members The VER file must be of the same name as the data file, residing in the same directory Throws on IO/reading/parsing/mismatch errors
- property System.Boolean AllowAga155CurrentRatingMismatch { get; set; }
  Allows engineering comparisons between AGA155 2A06 and 2A10 FPGA images (current codes 6 and 10). Defaults to false. Requires matching type 1/subtype 0x0150 and preserves all other identity checks. Does not allow unknown current identities; AllowForce retains its separate unknown-identity semantics.
- property System.Boolean AllowForce { get; set; }
  a user-set property that specifies whether to allow force FPGA download in case of: 1. Version mismatch, when the Remote Unit reports 'NA' (0), but VER file indicates a valid version 2. Remote Unit is Disconnected from the Master (CiStatus[1] != 3)
- property System.Int32 AmpVersion { get; }
  The remote FPGA file is only for this Remote Unit Amplifier Version ('0' means NA)
- property System.String AmpVersionStr { get; }
  Remote Unit Amplifier Version string representation
- field System.String BIN = .bin
  PH1P remote FPGA image extension: the TD bitstream, written to the remote's SPI flash as is
- property System.Int32 CommVersion { get; }
  The remote FPGA file is only for this Remote Unit Comm Version ('0' means NA)
- property System.String CommVersionStr { get; }
  Remote Unit Comm Version string representation
- property System.String DataFileName { get; }
  The RPD (MAX10) or BIN (PH1P) data file used at CTOR
- property System.String FPGASize { get; }
  Remote FPGA 'size' identifier: 4K, 8K, 16K or 60K
- property System.String FPGAVersion { get; }
  Remote FPGA Version string, i.e. 2.4.3 or 4.2.2.9-6 (ALPHA)
- property System.Boolean IsBinImage { get; }
  True for a PH1P .bin image; the remote must then report the PH1P FPGA family
- property System.Int32 Port { get; set; }
  a user-set property to indicate the target download Port index (i.e. 'A' = '0', 'B' = '1', etc.)
- field System.String RPD = .rpd
  Remote FPGA binary file extension
- method static System.String ReadDataFileExtension(AAComm.CommAPI, System.Int32)
  Reads which data file the remote FPGA on port takes, from its FEATURES block: BIN when it reports the PH1P family, RPD for every other remote (MAX10, or an image that predates the family field). The download refuses any other file with the same rule. Needs a connected api and a connected remote unit; throws when an offline read fails.
- field System.String Size16K = 16K
  string describing the FPGA model size "16K"
- field System.String Size4K = 4K
  string describing the FPGA model size "4K"
- field System.String Size60K = 60K
  string describing the FPGA model size "60K" (Anlogic PH1P50, .bin image)
- field System.String Size8K = 8K
  string describing the FPGA model size "8K"
- property System.Int32 UnitSubType { get; }
  The remote FPGA only for this Remote Unit Type/SubType
- property System.Int32 UnitType { get; }
  The remote FPGA only for this Remote Unit Type/SubType
- property System.Int32 Variant { get; }
  The remote FPGA file is only for this Remote Unit Variant ('0' means NA)
- property System.String VariantStr { get; }
  Remote Unit Variant string representation
- property System.String VersionFileName { get; }
  The accompanying Remote FPGA Version file

Class ParamHandlingSummary (AAComm.Extensions; AAComm C#): Summary of a parameter upload or download operation.
Signature: class AAComm.Extensions.ParamHandlingSummary

Members:
- ctor .ctor()
- property System.Boolean Canceled { get; }
  True if the operation was canceled by the caller (reserved for future use).
- property System.UInt16 Checksum { get; }
  File checksum (upload only). '0' if not available.
- property System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList<AAComm.Extensions.ParamConversion> Conversions { get; }
  Every download row whose value was rewritten before sending, as read and as sent (download only). Empty when none was.
- property System.Double ElapsedSeconds { get; }
  Wall-clock time of the entire handling, in seconds.
- property System.Int32 ErrorCount { get; }
  Number of parameters that produced an error reply.
- property System.String FPGAVersion { get; }
  Controller FPGA version string (upload only).
- property System.String FirmwareVersion { get; }
  Controller firmware version string (upload only).
- property System.Int32 ProductType { get; }
  Controller product type ID, as reported by ProductType.
- property System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList<AAComm.Extensions.ParamRejection> Rejections { get; }
  Every entry that was skipped or whose reply was classified as an error. Empty when there were none. On a download the first SkippedCount entries are the skipped rows, each answered by a PC Suite: ERR reason in the controller's place, because they are all added before anything is sent; the entries after them are controller replies, in send order. Not every one reached the controller: a client-side gate (User Units configuration, say) refuses some before the wire and answers in the controller's place.
- property System.Int32 SkippedCount { get; }
  Parameters that were skipped (download only: lines the reader dropped, entries the connected controller does not support, and withheld rows). Each one is named in Rejections.
- property System.Int32 SuccessCount { get; }
  Number of parameters processed without error.
- property System.Int32 TotalCount { get; }
  Total number of parameters processed (or attempted).

Class RecParamsResolver (AAComm.Extensions.RecData; AAComm C#): Resolves recording parameter names and header version based on the connected controller capabilities.
Signature: class AAComm.Extensions.RecData.RecParamsResolver

Members:
- ctor .ctor(AAComm.Interfaces.ICommService, System.Int32 = 1)
  MUST be used when API is CONNECTED! recSysID: 1 = RecDataA (default), 2 = RecDataB (Data Rec Snapshot)
- property System.Boolean AdvancedRecSupported { get; }
  Whether the connected controller supports the advanced recording protocol (V3)
- property System.Boolean DoubleSupported { get; }
  Whether the controller supports double-precision floating-point parameters
- method System.String GetRecUploadNext(System.Int32)
  Returns the RecUploadNext command string for the given step index (1 = init, 2 = next packet)
- method System.Int32 GetTriggerIndex(System.Int32)
  Returns the global 1-based trigger index for the given local trigger ID (1-based) within this recording system. For RecSysID=1: returns trigID as-is. For RecSysID=2: offsets by MaxNumOfTriggers.
- method System.Int32 GetTriggerLogicIndex(System.Int32)
  Returns the global 1-based logic connection index for the given local logic ID (1 or 2) within this recording system. For RecSysID=1: returns logicID as-is. For RecSysID=2: offsets by (MaxNumOfTriggers - 1).
- method static System.Boolean HeaderV1(System.Int32)
  LEGACY support: resolves whether connected controller uses RecUpload 'V1' protocol that supports only 8 recording parameters
- method static System.Boolean HeaderV3(AAComm.Services.ControllerMessagesContainer)
  Resolves whether a controller supports the 'V3' (advanced) recording protocol based on its messages container. V3 requires both RecDataB and RecTrigsLogic support.
- property System.String RecData { get; }
  Recording data command keyword (e.g. "RecData", "RecDataA")
- property System.String RecDataNumOfRecordedPoints { get; }
  Command string to query the points-recorded progress counter (e.g. "RecData[25]" or "RecDataA[3]")
- property System.String RecDataNumOfRequestedPoints { get; }
  Command string to query the progress denominator, numVectors * recLength from RecStart or the actual recorded length after a triggered RecStop (e.g. "RecData[1]" or "RecDataA[1]")
- property System.String RecGap { get; }
  Recording gap command keyword
- property System.String RecLength { get; }
