Class AACommPushMsgPushEvents (AAComm.Services.PushData; AAComm C#): SOURCE == 2 (push events): For VERSION_DATA = 1, the DATA section contains raw binary data (little-endian) with fixed-size event records. Binary packet structure (after the header, before the records): - uint8 n: number of event records - uint16 missed: events dropped since the last successful flush - uint16 freeRows: remaining free rows in the controller's event queue - uint16 reserved: zero Then n times, exactly 50 bytes each: - uint8 type: event type - uint8 axis: axis or port, NoAxis when controller-wide - uint32 timeSec: seconds since power-on - uint32 timeTick: sub-second tick - double data1..data5: type-specific values DATA is validated by arithmetic: it must be exactly 7 + 50n bytes. The packet terminator ('>' CR) may follow it, because the binary IPC path delivers the controller's bytes untrimmed.
Signature: class AAComm.Services.PushData.AACommPushMsgPushEvents

