Struct aacomm_connection (aacomm.h; AAComm C): Connection descriptor. Zero-initialize, then set the fields for your channel. Fields left 0 fall back to library defaults, EXCEPT: - channel_type is always honored, - can_channel (0 is a valid CAN channel, copied verbatim for CAN), - ip1..ip4 are ONE field of four octets: all four 0 = library default IP; anything else is used verbatim (so real addresses with zero octets, e.g. 10.0.0.5, work). controller_type: aacomm_connect requires it to match the connected controller, else AACOMM_RESULT_INVALID_CONTROLLER_TYPE. Set it explicitly, or leave it 0 and call aacomm_test_connection first, which writes the detected type back here. Field order/size must match the library's struct exactly.
